{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2156-04-10 14:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Lee, one of your nephrology team members. I understand you came in today because your kidney function was off during your clinic visit?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2156-04-10 14:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. My creatinine was higher than usual—2.9 instead of my normal 1.7. But I feel fine, no symptoms at all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2156-04-10 14:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good you’re feeling well. But a jump like that does raise concern, especially with your history. We’re admitting you to check for possible rejection of your transplant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2156-04-10 14:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Rejection? I thought I was stable. I’ve been careful with my meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2156-04-10 14:20:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You have been, and that helps a lot. But sometimes rejection can happen even when we’re doing everything right. We’ll do an ultrasound first to look at the kidney."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2156-04-10 16:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The ultrasound is back. There’s mild hydronephrosis—some swelling in the kidney—and the blood flow looks a bit stiff. That supports the need to look closer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2156-04-10 16:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Swelling? Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2156-04-10 16:48:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s mild, so not an emergency, but it’s a clue. We still need a biopsy to know for sure what’s going on. We’ll do that tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2156-04-10 16:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A biopsy? Is that risky?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2156-04-10 16:51:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a small needle biopsy, guided by ultrasound. Very safe. We’ll take a tiny piece of the kidney to examine under the microscope."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2156-04-11 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re all set for the biopsy. You’ll lie on your stomach, and we’ll use the ultrasound to guide the needle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2156-04-11 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready. Just tell me what to do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2156-04-11 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All done. Two samples were taken, sent to pathology. You’ll need to lie flat for a few hours to prevent bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2156-04-11 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That wasn’t so bad. How long until we know the results?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2156-04-11 10:18:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We should have preliminary findings by tomorrow, full report in a few days. We’ll start watching your labs closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2156-04-12 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The biopsy shows acute humoral rejection. That means your immune system is attacking the kidney, even though you’re on anti-rejection meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2156-04-12 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no. I lost my first kidney to rejection. I don’t want to lose this one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2156-04-12 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to treat this aggressively to protect it. We’ll start plasmapheresis—cleaning antibodies out of your blood—and high-dose steroids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2156-04-12 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Plasma-what? That sounds intense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2156-04-12 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It is, but it’s standard for this type of rejection. We’ll place a temporary catheter in your neck to run the treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2156-04-12 08:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The catheter is in—right internal jugular. You’ll start plasmapheresis this afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2156-04-12 08:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s in already? I didn’t feel much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2156-04-12 08:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You were given some sedation. You’ll have sessions every other day. We’re also starting IV steroids—500 mg daily for three days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2156-04-13 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling this morning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2156-04-13 07:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A bit jittery. And I’m hungry, but my blood sugar was high this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2156-04-13 07:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The steroids can raise blood sugar. We’re starting glipizide twice a day and will check your sugars four times daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2156-04-13 07:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve never had diabetes. Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2156-04-13 07:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not necessarily. It might improve as we lower the steroid dose. We’ll monitor closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2156-04-14 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure has been running high—around 165/90. We think it’s from the steroids and fluid from plasmapheresis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2156-04-14 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve always had high BP, but it’s usually controlled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2156-04-14 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re increasing your labetalol to 600 mg three times a day and adding furosemide 20 mg twice daily to help with fluid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2156-04-14 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I have noticed my ankles are a little puffy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2156-04-15 07:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had your second plasmapheresis. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2156-04-15 07:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Tired, but my breathing feels better. Less tight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2156-04-15 07:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good—that’s probably the fluid coming down. Your BP is improving too, now around 140s/80s."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2156-04-16 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is still high—2.7—and not coming down as fast as we’d like."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2156-04-16 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Does that mean the treatment isn’t working?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2156-04-16 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not necessarily. We’re adding a medication called ATG—anti-thymocyte globulin—to further calm your immune system."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2156-04-16 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "More treatment? How many more things will I need?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2156-04-16 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just four doses, given over the next few days. It’s strong, so we’ll watch for side effects like fever or low blood counts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2156-04-17 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Starting your first ATG infusion today. We’ll go slowly and monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2156-04-17 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m a little nervous. Any chance of fever?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2156-04-17 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possible, but we’ll give pre-medications to reduce that risk. Let us know right away if you feel chills or warmth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2156-04-18 07:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re halfway through ATG. No fevers, which is great. But your white count is dropping—down to 2.8."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2156-04-18 07:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2156-04-18 07:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It means you’re more prone to infection. We’ll keep an eye on it, but it’s expected with this treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2156-04-19 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your third plasmapheresis is scheduled for today. Creatinine is still 2.6—stable but not improving yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2156-04-19 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m hoping it starts to come down soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2156-04-19 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We are too. The treatment takes time. The fact that you’re feeling well is a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2156-04-20 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final ATG dose given yesterday. You’ve tolerated it well. We’re switching to oral prednisone—20 mg daily—and tapering down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2156-04-20 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’ll be on steroids longer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2156-04-20 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but at a much lower dose than the IV. We’ll keep the glipizide and add Humalog insulin with meals to manage sugars."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2156-04-20 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Insulin? I really hope I don’t need that long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2156-04-20 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll reassess when steroids are lower. For now, it’s to keep your sugars safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2156-04-20 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning discharge tomorrow. You’ll go home with adjusted meds and close follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2156-04-20 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. What changes should I expect?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2156-04-20 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re increasing tacrolimus to 6.5 mg twice daily, stopping lisinopril, and continuing the new BP and diabetes meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2156-04-20 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the catheter?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2156-04-20 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It will be removed just before you leave. You won’t need it anymore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2156-04-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Final check before discharge. Your labs are stable, you’re feeling well, and the catheter is out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2156-04-21 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2156-04-21 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. Keep taking all meds as prescribed, log your blood sugars, and see your transplant team in one week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2156-04-21 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I just hope this kidney holds on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2156-04-21 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving it the best chance. You’ve been through a lot, but you’re on the right path."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2156-04-21 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I really appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2156-04-21 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call if you have fever, swelling, or blood sugar issues. We’re here for you."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2156-04-10 13:59:00",
    "admission_end": "2156-04-21 13:42:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for evaluation of elevated creatinine (2.9 mg/dL) from her baseline of 1.7, detected during a routine transplant clinic visit. She was asymptomatic. Ultrasound revealed mild hydronephrosis and elevated resistive indices, prompting a kidney biopsy which confirmed acute humoral rejection. Treatment included plasmapheresis with a tunneled catheter, high-dose IV steroids tapered to oral prednisone, and four doses of ATG. Due to steroid-induced hyperglycemia, glipizide and Humalog insulin were initiated. Hypertension, worsened by fluid overload and steroids, was managed by increasing labetalol and adding furosemide, while lisinopril was held. Tacrolimus was increased to 6.5 mg twice daily. The patient remained stable, with creatinine plateauing at 2.6 mg/dL. She was discharged home with medication adjustments and close follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Complications of transplanted kidney",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Hydronephrosis",
      "Other fluid overload",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Other abnormal glucose",
      "Anemia, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
